  (:adr/decision-summary
  (vector "D1: A static-clean revision remains quarantined until a networkless, read-only, no-new-privileges scanner returns a passing receipt after a real bounded load"
   "D2: Approved GGUF promotion is pull-based and reaches the fleet SSoT canary asher; it requires checksum, disk-headroom, inference-health, persistent-service, and rollback evidence before deployed"
   "D3: Scanner and fleet bearer authority is separate from user JWT, publisher, and moderator authority"
   "D4: Trust cases and appeals are typed, actor-attributed, evidence-linked, and human-decided; ordinary reports never become automatic legal judgments"
   "D5: The production boundary is cloud-murakumo merge 100e632e1845335676b3430b68daa6248414616a, D1 migration 0005, Worker version 5e13d584-9977-4861-bbf9-5b71535a3cc9, and two live operator LaunchAgents"))

  (:adr/verify
  (vector "curl https://murakumo.cloud/api/v1/model-hosting | jq .phase_4"
   "wrangler d1 migrations list murakumo-model-registry --remote"
   "launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/cloud.murakumo.model-scanner"
   "launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/cloud.murakumo.model-fleet"
   "ssh asher '/opt/homebrew/bin/llama-cli --version'"))

  (:adr/body
  "# Context

Phase 2/3 supplied public repositories, revisions, cards, licenses, provenance,
private/gated access, community objects, static quarantine and governed promotion.
Three operational gaps remained: there was no real fleet target, no dynamic model
load boundary, and no dedicated copyright/license/takedown/appeal workflow.

# Decision

Uploaded bytes never execute in the Cloudflare Worker. Static-clean revisions enter
a pull queue. A pinned Linux container loads safetensors, ONNX or GGUF without a
network and with a read-only root, dropped capabilities and bounded resources. ONNX
and GGUF execute bounded inference; any load, inference or finite-output failure is
fail-closed.

Approved GGUF revisions enter a second pull queue. The operator verifies the file
again, transfers it to `asher`, starts a loopback-only canary, performs at least 20
real probes, and only then installs the fixed root-owned LaunchDaemon. The prior
revision target is retained for rollback. Repository metadata cannot supply argv or
commands. ONNX and safetensors remain scan-supported but deployment-unsupported.

Trust operations use typed cases, append-only actor events, emergency containment,
legal hold and owner appeal. Malware/CSAM reports receive emergency priority, but an
ordinary reporter cannot quarantine content. Copyright/license/privacy claims need
a good-faith declaration and human adjudication. An accepted appeal does not restore
content without a separate moderator restore decision.

# Evidence

`cloud-murakumo` PR #50 merged as `100e632`. A live 64,488,992-byte tiny GGUF passed
transfer checksum, load, canary inference, persistent production inference and
rollback on `asher`; the smoke service and weights were removed afterward. The
scanner container passed safetensors and ONNX repeatable tests and a live GGUF load.
D1 migration 0005 and Worker version `5e13d584-9977-4861-bbf9-5b71535a3cc9` are live.
Both operator pollers are running with a Keychain-held operations token.

# Remaining boundaries

Private/gated bytes are access-controlled, not encrypted. There is no ONNX or
safetensors fleet deployment adapter, cross-region replication, jurisdiction-specific
mandatory-reporting integration, or automatic legal ownership determination.")
))
